    },
    {
      "question": "How does the performance of SVE/SVE2 compare to NEON for different block sizes in SSD and Hadamard transforms?",
      "answer": "The benchmarks show that SVE/SVE2 consistently outperforms NEON across all tested block sizes. For SSD, the largest block (4x16) saw a 2.6× speedup on Yitian 710 and a 1.5× improvement on Graviton3. In the Hadamard AC kernel, the 16x16 block achieved a 1.35× speedup on Yitian 710 and a 1.23× improvement on Graviton3. Even for smaller blocks like 4x4, SVE/SVE2 was competitive with NEON, sometimes matching its speed (ssd_8x4_sve = ssd_8x4_neon). These numbers illustrate that SVE/SVE2 scales well with larger data widths, providing consistent gains across a range of transform sizes.\n#### SVE/SVE2 delivers 1.2×–3.8× speedups over NEON, especially for larger block sizes.",
