      "answer": "ARM64 provides a dedicated rounded right shift instruction that automatically adds the appropriate rounding bias before shifting. By using this instruction instead of manually adding a constant via a fused multiply‑add, the code eliminates an extra arithmetic operation and simplifies the instruction stream. Benchmarks show that this change yields a 3% speedup on Cortex A53, about 8% on Cortex A72/A73 for 8‑bit per channel dequantization, and between 10–20% on A72/A73 for 10‑bit per channel. These gains come from fewer instructions and better pipeline utilization.\n#### Using a rounded right shift removes an extra add and speeds dequant by up to 20%"
